Subject: [PATCH 06904/11362] [outer-loop] g50t: L5 SOLVED round 7 (codex,
 second assembly by analogy)

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session resolved the second color-11 assembly by
exact analogy with the first (round 6 correctly identified this as the
concrete next step). After the first socket traversal, RIGHTx3, DOWNx3
reaches the second far socket while clone A traverses its control;
continuing RIGHTx3 reaches a remote color-15 endpoint committed as
clone B. The final runner repeats the dual-socket route, then
DOWNx2, RIGHT enters the upper elevator synchronized on clone B's
endpoint tick, carried to the lower car, exiting onto the goal.

Full winning sequence: 204 actions. The source agent's own
fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed reached_level=5. The
outer loop independently re-verified regardless -- and found g50t has
TWO distinct label-applier functions registered in this codebase (the
generic GameAdapter expects JSON-dict labels; the resolver's actual
registered function, exp4433.apply_g50t_label, expects bare integers
with a retry loop). Using the resolver-registered function (the
authoritative one), 5x fresh env.reset() + replay all confirmed
level=5, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: g50t levels_reproduced 4 -> 5.
reproducible_total_levels 161 -> 162 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
